From f3da535429f31bb6de80db197c23bf2735c242ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:18:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(safe-edit): bind verified bidirectional sync proof to the
 daemon child

The Safe Edit gate re-derived its proof from the 500-line in-memory log on
every apply, so a healthy, verified, idle daemon was held once the wrapper's
one-time "[sync-policy] Verified bidirectional sync." line rotated out. It
also accepted that line from anywhere in the log (note(), stdout, later ob
output), so it could be forged.

The supervisor now records proof only when the head of the current child's
own stderr is that exact line (after at most Node runtime warnings), which
the wrapper prints before it spawns ob. Proof lives as long as that child:
it is dropped on stop, resetAndStart (re-auth/relink), exit, backoff and
any new spawn. withPausedForEdit, single writer, CAS and permissions are
unchanged.

IOS-ORCH-RI-001

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
